00:41:21,818 --> 00:41:27,818
Shelby Oaks is a 2025 American supernatural horror mystery film produced, written, and directed by Chris
Stuckmann in his feature directorial debut, with Mike Flanagan as an executive producer.

11
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:36,000
It stars Camille Sullivan, Brendan Sexton III, Keith David, Sarah Durn, Derek Mears,
Emily Bennett, Charlie Talbert, Robin Bartlett, and Michael Beach.

12
00:49:38,181 --> 00:49:44,181
It follows a woman (Sullivan) determined to find her sister (Durn), who went missing
while investigating the mysterious abandoned town of Shelby Oaks.

13
00:53:46,363 --> 00:53:52,363
The story for Shelby Oaks was written by Stuckmann
and his wife, Samantha Elizabeth.

14
00:57:54,545 --> 00:58:00,545
An independent production, the film was crowdfunded through Kickstarter.

15
01:02:02,727 --> 01:02:08,727
By March 2022, it had become the most-funded horror film
on the platform after raising $650,000.

16
01:06:10,909 --> 01:06:16,909
Principal photography took place in Stuckmann's home state of Ohio in mid-2022.

17
01:10:19,090 --> 01:10:25,090
Shelby Oaks had its world premiere at the 28th Fantasia International Film Festival on July 20, 2024, after
which Flanagan became attached to the project, eventually becoming an executive producer.

18
01:14:27,272 --> 01:14:33,272
The film was subsequently re-edited and underwent reshoots before it
was released at Fantastic Fest in September 2025.

19
01:18:35,454 --> 01:18:41,454
The film was released theatrically in the United States by Neon on October 24, 2025, to
mixed reviews from critics and grossed $6 million at the box office.

